NAME
    clsave - save a recorded GL command list to a file

SYNOPSIS
    clsave n file

DESCRIPTION
    Reads GL command list n back from the card (the stage-10e CLRD
    verb) and writes its raw hex command bytes to file. The file is a
    pure hex-mode GL stream, so it replays directly:

        gl file                      draw it now
        gl CLBEG 3 + gl file + gl CLEND    ...or re-record it as a list

    With clsave, a scene built on the card -- tri's list 0, house's
    list 1, anything CLBEG recorded -- survives power: record, save,
    replay any day. An undefined list reports ?No such list.

    The read-back FIFO is small and the card stalls when it fills;
    clsave's drain loop is the flow control, so lists up to the full
    4KB slot save fine.

SEE ALSO
    gl, tri, house, man gl (CLRD, CLBEG/CLEND)
